+
+@opcode{contractioncasedword}
+For forward translation in mixed-script tables, treat a @code{contraction}
+rule as a complete cased-letter word when neither adjacent character is
+a digit or has an uppercase variant. A caseless character remains a
+boundary even when its definition uses the @code{lowercase} opcode.
+This affects shortform disambiguation with @code{nocontractsign} only;
+ordinary contraction and punctuation rules keep their existing boundaries.
+Without this option, @code{contraction} uses the normal sequence rules.
 
